    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0364" n="1042" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1042"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Pruyn</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-08-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 7, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatches Nos. 16 to 21, inclusive,
                    and those of your predecessor, numbered 13, 14, and 15, and one without number
                    dated May 6, have been received.</p>
                <p>The account you give of your flattering reception, as the successor of Mr.
                    Harris, is very gratifying, and tends to confirm the impression that the
                    friendly relations between the government of Japan and that of the United States
                    are in no danger of being disturbed.</p>
                <p>I enclose herewith a sealed communication addressed to their excellencies the
                    ministers for foreign affairs of the empire of Japan, a transcript of which, for
                    your information, is also herewith transmitted. The original you will deliver in
                    such manner as you may deem most proper.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert H. Pruyn</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., Yedo.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
